{"post_stream":{"posts":[{"id":485584,"name":"Matt","username":"Matt_Fuller1","avatar_template":"https://avatars.discourse-cdn.com/v4/letter/m/a587f6/{size}.png","created_at":"2026-09-07T16:43:52.949Z","cooked":"\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-485584-where-does-the-bug-appear-featureproduct-1\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-485584-where-does-the-bug-appear-featureproduct-1\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eWhere does the bug appear (feature/product)?\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eGrok Bot\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-485584-describe-the-bug-2\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-485584-describe-the-bug-2\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eDescribe the Bug\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eProduct: Grok Bot for macOS\u003cbr\u003e\nAccount: same Cursor / SuperGrok account used to sign in to the desktop app\u003cbr\u003e\nDate / timezone: Monday, September 7, 2026, America/Chicago (CDT)\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eSummary\u003cbr\u003e\nGrok Bot on Mac returns “AI Model Not Found.” The model string it tries to use is not valid: “grok-4-7-0907”. The error persists after the official recovery steps. There is no in-app “Report an issue” control.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eExact error\u003cbr\u003e\nAI Model Not Found\u003cbr\u003e\nModel name is not valid: “grok-4-7-0907”\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eSteps already tried\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003col\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eFully quit Grok Bot with Cmd+Q and reopen\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eSign out and sign back in\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eNew chat with the existing Bot\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eNew → Create new agent\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eConfirmed there is no model picker in Settings → General → Agent\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eConfirmed there is no in-app Report an issue option\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ol\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eResult\u003cbr\u003e\nSame error on existing Bots and on a new agent. Local app recovery does not change the model ID.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eNotes\u003cbr\u003e\ngrok-4-7-0907 looks like a dated Grok 4.7 snapshot. Grok 4.7 does not appear in the public model docs yet. This looks like a backend assignment to an unpublished model, not a corrupt local install.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eI can provide another screenshot, About panel text, or a new request ID if needed.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-485584-steps-to-reproduce-3\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-485584-steps-to-reproduce-3\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eSteps to Reproduce\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eGrok Bot on Mac returns “AI Model Not Found.” The model string it tries to use is not valid: “grok-4-7-0907”. The error persists after the official recovery steps. There is no in-app “Report an issue” control.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-485584-expected-behavior-4\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-485584-expected-behavior-4\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eExpected Behavior\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eExpecting a valid model.  Grok Bot to stop requesting grok-4-7-0907 and use a live assigned model again (currently documented flagship is grok-4.6). I cannot change the model myself. Official docs say Cursor manages model selection and there is no model picker.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-485584-operating-system-5\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-485584-operating-system-5\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eOperating System\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eMacOS\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-485584-version-information-6\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-485584-version-information-6\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eVersion Information\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eApp: Grok Bot for macOS\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eGrok Bot version: v0.44.0\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003emacOS version: macOS 26.6.2\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eChip: M1 Max - 64 GB RAM - 3 TB of SSD Available\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=